lege-football/story/_/id/50142903/jeremiah-smith-ohio-state-record-tracker","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Alabama makes last-second call to start QB Keelon Russell","description":"No. 3 Alabama made a last-second decision to start Keelon Russell against Vanderbilt after the quarterback looked better than anticipated in pregame warmups.","published":"2026-11-14T18:56:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50480988/alabama-makes-last-second-call-start-qb-keelon-russell","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Maryland QB Malik Washington doesn't start vs. Wisconsin","description":"Maryland quarterback Malik Washington did not start against Wisconsin as he continues to deal with a lower-body injury.","published":"2026-11-14T17:50:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50480722/source-maryland-qb-malik-washington-start-vs-wisconsin","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Colorado upsets No. 14 Houston for first AP top-15 win since 2007","description":"Colorado posted its first victory over an AP top-15 team since 2007 in beating No. 14 Houston 42-32 and slightly cooled down the hot seat for coach Deion Sanders.","published":"2026-11-14T14:22:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50479172/colorado-upsets-no-14-houston-1st-ap-top-15-win-2007","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Ole Miss-Oklahoma bumped to Sunday despite Sooners AD's 'strong objection'","description":"Oklahoma AD Roger Denny was critical of the SEC's decision to move the Sooners' home game against Ole Miss to Sunday following Friday's nationwide ground stop.","published":"2026-11-14T17:36:21.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50478281/ole-miss-oklahoma-bumped-sunday-sooners-ad-rips-decision","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Paolo Uggetti","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"UCLA QB Ty Dieffenbach says first-half shoulder injury vs. Illinois not serious","description":"UCLA starting quarterback Ty Dieffenbach exited because of a shoulder injury late in the second quarter but returned to lead the Bruins past Illinois 22-14.","published":"2026-11-14T17:06:41.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50477249/ucla-qb-ty-dieffenbach-leaves-game-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Paolo Uggetti","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest claims 'Bachelor U' status after Sam Hartman news","description":"Wake Forest football is the only program, the school says, to have had three former players feature in \"The Bachelor\" franchise.","published":"2026-11-13T23:57:20.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50475193/sam-hartman-bachelor-wake-forest","type":"Story","byline":"J.J. Post","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"FAA ground stop throws sports world into travel chaos ahead of weekend games","description":"Travel plans for teams in multiple sports were disrupted by the FAA's nationwide ground stop of all flights because of communications problems.","published":"2026-11-14T15:50:35.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50475169/faa-ground-stop-disrupting-travel-college-football-teams","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5138455/jide-abasiri","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jide_Abasiri"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jide Abasiri","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jide_Abasiri","description":"American football player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:38:11Z","intro":"Jide Abasiri (born March 10, 2006) is an American college football defensive tackle for the USC Trojans.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Abasiri attended Prior Lake High School in Savage, Minnesota. As a senior in 2023, he was named the team's defensive lineman of the year and The Minnesota Star Tribune All-Metro First Team after recording 57 tackles and two sacks. He played in the Minnesota High School All-Star Game. He originally committed to play college football at the University of Minnesota before flipping his commitment to the University of Southern California (USC)."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Abasiri played in 10 games as a true freshman at USC in 2024, recording seven tackles. As a sophomore in 2025, he started nine of 13 games and had 26 tackles and 3.5 sacks. Abasiri returned to USC as a starter his junior year in 2026."}]}}